BND-16: start a time-series evaporation on the entry in effect at the start date

When the simulation starts between two entries of the [EVAPORATION] TIMESERIES
series, climate_initState() scanned forward to the first entry on or after the
start date and used that entry's rate from the start. During the run each
entry applies from its own date, so the period from the start date to the next
entry got the next period's rate. Move instead to the last entry on or before
the start date and use its rate; the next entry then takes over at its date as
usual. Runs that start on or before the first entry are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-16_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
index c343b93..c4c0012 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
@@ -964,6 +964,9 @@ void climate_openFile()
  */
 void climate_initState()
 {
+    int i, n;
+    double d, e;
+
     LastDay = NO_DATE;
     Temp.tmax = MISSING;
     Temp.apiTemp = MISSING;
@@ -982,7 +985,16 @@ void climate_initState()
                             &NextEvapDate, &NextEvapRate);
         if (NextEvapDate < StartDate)
         {
-            setNextEvapDate(StartDate);
+            // --- move to the last entry on or before StartDate: its rate
+            //     is in effect until the next entry's date
+            n = 0;
+            while (table_getNextEntry(&Tseries[Evap.tSeries], &d, &e) &&
+                   d <= StartDate) n++;
+            table_getFirstEntry(&Tseries[Evap.tSeries],
+                                &NextEvapDate, &NextEvapRate);
+            for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
+                table_getNextEntry(&Tseries[Evap.tSeries],
+                                   &NextEvapDate, &NextEvapRate);
         }
         Evap.rate = NextEvapRate / UCF(EVAPRATE);
 
